[{:db/id "f100370d-dab2-5f2f-94c0-ca4059d2a5e5" :answer/id #uuid "f100370d-dab2-5f2f-94c0-ca4059d2a5e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-144" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1e419297-22b4-5144-949a-5be3e729d78c" :answer/id #uuid "1e419297-22b4-5144-949a-5be3e729d78c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-204" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1553423d-6619-5296-aa27-6dfa538e24eb" :answer/id #uuid "1553423d-6619-5296-aa27-6dfa538e24eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "78" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "fa06d295-a30b-5d75-a328-9f9ffade51bf" :answer/id #uuid "fa06d295-a30b-5d75-a328-9f9ffade51bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-84" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5bcd6ddb-a207-5fad-a229-e213b01e5b8b" :answer/id #uuid "5bcd6ddb-a207-5fad-a229-e213b01e5b8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c8ed3c28-7663-5d3f-a250-39410e6adb51" :answer-field/id #uuid "c8ed3c28-7663-5d3f-a250-39410e6adb51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["f100370d-dab2-5f2f-94c0-ca4059d2a5e5" "1e419297-22b4-5144-949a-5be3e729d78c" "1553423d-6619-5296-aa27-6dfa538e24eb" "fa06d295-a30b-5d75-a328-9f9ffade51bf" "5bcd6ddb-a207-5fad-a229-e213b01e5b8b"] :answer-field/correct "fa06d295-a30b-5d75-a328-9f9ffade51bf" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "a445e341-e46b-5bbe-83fe-c9e1dc16e770" :question/id #uuid "a445e341-e46b-5bbe-83fe-c9e1dc16e770" :question/problem "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y)=3 x^{2} - 3 y^{2}$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)=⟨- 3 t + 2,2 t - 1⟩$ at the point $t=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of $f(x,y)$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)$ is given by $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$ To calculate this, we can use the chain rule.\n\nThe chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3 x^{2} - 3 y^{2}),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3 x^{2} - 3 y^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6 x,- 6 y⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=- 3 t + 2$, $y=2 t - 1$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =⟨6 \\left(- 3 t + 2\\right),- 6 \\left(2 t - 1\\right)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 18 t + 12,- 12 t + 6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 3 t + 2),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t - 1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨- 18 t + 12,- 12 t + 6⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\left(- 18 t + 12\\right)\\cdot \\left(-3\\right)+\\left(- 12 t + 6\\right)\\cdot \\left(2\\right) \\\\  & =30 t - 24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $r(t)$ at $t=-2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(-2))] & =30 (-2) - 24 \\\\  & =-84.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["c8ed3c28-7663-5d3f-a250-39410e6adb51"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "c61528ae-e201-5472-8074-86f9a0167d35" :answer/id #uuid "c61528ae-e201-5472-8074-86f9a0167d35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-30" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "975a5f2c-7188-5d8c-9367-ea71bf9eb231" :answer/id #uuid "975a5f2c-7188-5d8c-9367-ea71bf9eb231" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1da546db-3c69-539d-8533-ef14ece2b34c" :answer/id #uuid "1da546db-3c69-539d-8533-ef14ece2b34c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-24" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2fc09648-34f1-5455-b38a-edf896692a5d" :answer/id #uuid "2fc09648-34f1-5455-b38a-edf896692a5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4bb3978c-e581-51df-8b00-a1c1601ddca9" :answer/id #uuid "4bb3978c-e581-51df-8b00-a1c1601ddca9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c26508b5-c575-52f3-b001-a3bcc480b401" :answer-field/id #uuid "c26508b5-c575-52f3-b001-a3bcc480b401" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["c61528ae-e201-5472-8074-86f9a0167d35" "975a5f2c-7188-5d8c-9367-ea71bf9eb231" "1da546db-3c69-539d-8533-ef14ece2b34c" "2fc09648-34f1-5455-b38a-edf896692a5d" "4bb3978c-e581-51df-8b00-a1c1601ddca9"] :answer-field/correct "4bb3978c-e581-51df-8b00-a1c1601ddca9" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "9dcc91d6-8511-52d2-b88b-562fac2dd7c9" :question/id #uuid "9dcc91d6-8511-52d2-b88b-562fac2dd7c9" :question/problem "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y)=- 3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2}$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)=⟨- t + 2,2 t⟩$ at the point $t=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of $f(x,y)$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)$ is given by $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$ To calculate this, we can use the chain rule.\n\nThe chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2}),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 6 x,6 y⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=- t + 2$, $y=2 t$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =⟨- 6 \\left(- t + 2\\right),6 \\cdot 2 t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6 t - 12,12 t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- t + 2),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨6 t - 12,12 t⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\left(6 t - 12\\right)\\cdot \\left(-1\\right)+\\left(12 t\\right)\\cdot \\left(2\\right) \\\\  & =18 t + 12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $r(t)$ at $t=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(-1))] & =18 (-1) + 12 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["c26508b5-c575-52f3-b001-a3bcc480b401"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "51c65ed2-f0a3-5583-90c1-01d3b3865b32" :answer/id #uuid "51c65ed2-f0a3-5583-90c1-01d3b3865b32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7c87e7bb-1e6b-5577-9c25-5750c2d40b40" :answer/id #uuid "7c87e7bb-1e6b-5577-9c25-5750c2d40b40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4ae7aec4-1d83-5eea-8940-6f5cbdb71e5f" :answer/id #uuid "4ae7aec4-1d83-5eea-8940-6f5cbdb71e5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6b912948-1642-5e4e-a34a-7231c206e0a5" :answer/id #uuid "6b912948-1642-5e4e-a34a-7231c206e0a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-24" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "370db119-3661-5ef2-b2af-6ee498d06182" :answer/id #uuid "370db119-3661-5ef2-b2af-6ee498d06182" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "3a9d6bbb-fcd7-51d9-a68b-5d578c88f08e" :answer-field/id #uuid "3a9d6bbb-fcd7-51d9-a68b-5d578c88f08e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["51c65ed2-f0a3-5583-90c1-01d3b3865b32" "7c87e7bb-1e6b-5577-9c25-5750c2d40b40" "4ae7aec4-1d83-5eea-8940-6f5cbdb71e5f" "6b912948-1642-5e4e-a34a-7231c206e0a5" "370db119-3661-5ef2-b2af-6ee498d06182"] :answer-field/correct "4ae7aec4-1d83-5eea-8940-6f5cbdb71e5f" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "de3e4415-7d66-5c90-8a1e-b6b9a369cc6a" :question/id #uuid "de3e4415-7d66-5c90-8a1e-b6b9a369cc6a" :question/problem "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y)=- 3 x^{2} - 2 y^{2}$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)=⟨t - 2,3 t + 2⟩$ at the point $t=0.$" :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of $f(x,y)$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)$ is given by $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$ To calculate this, we can use the chain rule.\n\nThe chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 3 x^{2} - 2 y^{2}),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 3 x^{2} - 2 y^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 6 x,- 4 y⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t - 2$, $y=3 t + 2$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =⟨- 6 \\left(t - 2\\right),- 4 \\left(3 t + 2\\right)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 6 t + 12,- 12 t - 8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t - 2),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 t + 2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨- 6 t + 12,- 12 t - 8⟩\\cdot ⟨1,3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left(- 6 t + 12\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)+\\left(- 12 t - 8\\right)\\cdot \\left(3\\right) \\\\  & =- 42 t - 12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $r(t)$ at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(0))] & =- 42 (0) - 12 \\\\  & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["3a9d6bbb-fcd7-51d9-a68b-5d578c88f08e"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "a190bb06-3da8-5c89-b3a7-dafbff724ab9" :answer/id #uuid "a190bb06-3da8-5c89-b3a7-dafbff724ab9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-40" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c9250b77-adfa-55a2-9bc2-f29bce32c28f" :answer/id #uuid "c9250b77-adfa-55a2-9bc2-f29bce32c28f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "64f6d064-4d09-5ab2-acff-66f1b85596b3" :answer/id #uuid "64f6d064-4d09-5ab2-acff-66f1b85596b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "10a2909f-aed0-5af2-b387-7f8903415e75" :answer/id #uuid "10a2909f-aed0-5af2-b387-7f8903415e75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-42" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a74ba907-6998-5a4f-b6f4-82147ccc7fff" :answer/id #uuid "a74ba907-6998-5a4f-b6f4-82147ccc7fff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-44" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7a7b6273-78bd-5548-919c-67a2237339f3" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a7b6273-78bd-5548-919c-67a2237339f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["a190bb06-3da8-5c89-b3a7-dafbff724ab9" "c9250b77-adfa-55a2-9bc2-f29bce32c28f" "64f6d064-4d09-5ab2-acff-66f1b85596b3" "10a2909f-aed0-5af2-b387-7f8903415e75" "a74ba907-6998-5a4f-b6f4-82147ccc7fff"] :answer-field/correct "a190bb06-3da8-5c89-b3a7-dafbff724ab9" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "a6d7ded6-d4bb-5d2b-990f-e6ceb3a10aad" :question/id #uuid "a6d7ded6-d4bb-5d2b-990f-e6ceb3a10aad" :question/problem "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y)=x^{2} - y^{2}$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)=⟨- 3 t + 1,- t - 1⟩$ at the point $t=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of $f(x,y)$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)$ is given by $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$ To calculate this, we can use the chain rule.\n\nThe chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2} - y^{2}),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x^{2} - y^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 x,- 2 y⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=- 3 t + 1$, $y=- t - 1$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =⟨2 \\left(- 3 t + 1\\right),- 2 \\left(- t - 1\\right)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 6 t + 2,2 t + 2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 3 t + 1),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- t - 1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨- 6 t + 2,2 t + 2⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left(- 6 t + 2\\right)\\cdot \\left(-3\\right)+\\left(2 t + 2\\right)\\cdot \\left(-1\\right) \\\\  & =16 t - 8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $r(t)$ at $t=-2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(-2))] & =16 (-2) - 8 \\\\  & =-40.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["7a7b6273-78bd-5548-919c-67a2237339f3"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "35332580-e736-51f3-8d53-d1689267dc18" :answer/id #uuid "35332580-e736-51f3-8d53-d1689267dc18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-24" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "64ffb12f-f951-5c6b-b7c6-f1807ed116e7" :answer/id #uuid "64ffb12f-f951-5c6b-b7c6-f1807ed116e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ffc659a3-2842-5233-9d8a-956412977c32" :answer/id #uuid "ffc659a3-2842-5233-9d8a-956412977c32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "fc9688b1-f72b-59ba-9294-79661d37c55d" :answer/id #uuid "fc9688b1-f72b-59ba-9294-79661d37c55d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "745617d4-dbef-5347-9b3e-2ab7c6bdb0de" :answer/id #uuid "745617d4-dbef-5347-9b3e-2ab7c6bdb0de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-22" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2856210c-b0bb-5727-a27f-b36c68c9cded" :answer-field/id #uuid "2856210c-b0bb-5727-a27f-b36c68c9cded" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["35332580-e736-51f3-8d53-d1689267dc18" "64ffb12f-f951-5c6b-b7c6-f1807ed116e7" "ffc659a3-2842-5233-9d8a-956412977c32" "fc9688b1-f72b-59ba-9294-79661d37c55d" "745617d4-dbef-5347-9b3e-2ab7c6bdb0de"] :answer-field/correct "745617d4-dbef-5347-9b3e-2ab7c6bdb0de" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "53b4c038-e54a-5606-9304-0b269648dd21" :question/id #uuid "53b4c038-e54a-5606-9304-0b269648dd21" :question/problem "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y)=x^{2} - 2 y^{2}$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)=⟨t,- 3 t + 1⟩$ at the point $t=1.$" :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of $f(x,y)$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)$ is given by $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$ To calculate this, we can use the chain rule.\n\nThe chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2} - 2 y^{2}),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x^{2} - 2 y^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 x,- 4 y⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t$, $y=- 3 t + 1$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =⟨2 t,- 4 \\left(- 3 t + 1\\right)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 t,12 t - 4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 3 t + 1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨2 t,12 t - 4⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left(2 t\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)+\\left(12 t - 4\\right)\\cdot \\left(-3\\right) \\\\  & =- 34 t + 12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $r(t)$ at $t=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(1))] & =- 34 (1) + 12 \\\\  & =-22.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["2856210c-b0bb-5727-a27f-b36c68c9cded"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "cbbf1f2f-d0d2-572a-ab55-c1c9222d13d1" :answer/id #uuid "cbbf1f2f-d0d2-572a-ab55-c1c9222d13d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "dad22b74-b2c5-5810-9eb2-eca3707c010c" :answer/id #uuid "dad22b74-b2c5-5810-9eb2-eca3707c010c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-117" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "629864ea-dc15-5e3b-9b4d-74b9fb756902" :answer/id #uuid "629864ea-dc15-5e3b-9b4d-74b9fb756902" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-114" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8fc460a8-2b92-564e-84d2-f6bf88156beb" :answer/id #uuid "8fc460a8-2b92-564e-84d2-f6bf88156beb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-81" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e076ef3c-3f88-5355-bd0b-9db9eadc6d9b" :answer/id #uuid "e076ef3c-3f88-5355-bd0b-9db9eadc6d9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-72" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e46b8795-1350-500a-80d1-15be94df06e3" :answer-field/id #uuid "e46b8795-1350-500a-80d1-15be94df06e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["cbbf1f2f-d0d2-572a-ab55-c1c9222d13d1" "dad22b74-b2c5-5810-9eb2-eca3707c010c" "629864ea-dc15-5e3b-9b4d-74b9fb756902" "8fc460a8-2b92-564e-84d2-f6bf88156beb" "e076ef3c-3f88-5355-bd0b-9db9eadc6d9b"] :answer-field/correct "8fc460a8-2b92-564e-84d2-f6bf88156beb" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "034848a3-a1f9-5d8f-b396-bccbb706e96e" :question/id #uuid "034848a3-a1f9-5d8f-b396-bccbb706e96e" :question/problem "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y,z)=3 x z^{2} - 3 y^{3}$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)=⟨- 3 t,3,\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}⟩$ at the point $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)$ is given by $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$ To calculate this, we can use the chain rule.\n\nThe chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3 x z^{2} - 3 y^{3}),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3 x z^{2} - 3 y^{3}),\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3 x z^{2} - 3 y^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3 z^{2},- 9 y^{2},6 x z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=- 3 t$, $y=3$, $z=\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =⟨3 \\left(\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}\\right)^{2},- 9 \\cdot 3^{2},6 \\left(- 3 t\\right) \\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3 t^{2} - 9,-81,- 18 t \\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 3 t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨3 t^{2} - 9,-81,- 18 t \\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,0,\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\left(3 t^{2} - 9\\right)\\cdot \\left(-3\\right)+\\left(-81\\right)\\cdot \\left(0\\right)+\\left(- 18 t \\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}}\\right) \\\\  & =- 9 t^{2} + 27+0- 18 t^{2} \\\\  & =- 27 t^{2} + 27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $r(t)$ at $t=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(2))] & =- 27 (2)^{2} + 27 \\\\  & =-9+0-72 \\\\  & =-81.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["e46b8795-1350-500a-80d1-15be94df06e3"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "fbb1f922-a648-5